comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T00:42:27.383Z",codex-sol,"Baseline evidence: failing Ubuntu job 121400153960, CI run 40269872574: 21 passed, 11 failed. Release notes for v2026.10.22 explicitly document GH-1534 root relationship evidence retention and GH-1535 matching-population test health. v2026.10.23 contains no additional relationship changes. Comparing implementation and captured outputs to those contracts."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:19.074Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: context_blocked_fallback_deep_matches_oracle|GH-1535: add scope matching_active_items and total_items=0 for a blocked-only population."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:23.518Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: context_completion_rounding_matches_oracle|GH-1535: total_items=172 counts the complete active population even with focus limit 1; preserve completion rounding."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:30.245Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: context_matches_oracle|GH-1535: declare test-health scope and denominator, including zero for empty or terminal-only populations."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:34.054Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: context_sections_match_oracle|GH-1535: compute linked tests, stored runs and failing IDs over all matching active items before focus pagination and packing."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:37.139Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: padded_inverse_blockers_match_oracle|GH-1535: tests denominator includes one matching active item; preserve padded inverse blocker resolution."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:40.494Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: real_copy_harness_accepts_matching_packet_refusals|GH-1534: new producer-bounds receipt and root evidence packing alter rendered JSON floor advice; preserve exact stderr comparison."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:45.537Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: relationship_external_namespaces_match_oracle|GH-1534: prioritize direct prerequisite endpoints before optional external related nodes; preserve external key namespaces."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:51.808Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: relationship_large_edge_limit_finishes_at_budget_floor|GH-1534: include bounded receipt in rendered floor probes; captured feasible/minimum floor changes 331 to 348."
  "2026-10-27T00:44:58.116Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: relationship_packet_refusals_match_oracle|GH-1534: rendered TOON retry budget changes 392 to 448; recompute from the preserved query rather than hardcode."
  "2026-10-27T00:45:01.662Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: relationship_packets_match_oracle|GH-1534: reserve direct edge costs, emit root incident edges first, prioritize prerequisite and ancestor endpoints, version the cursor packing policy, and disclose traversal bounds."
  "2026-10-27T00:45:06.781Z",codex-sol,"Classification (a), intentional upstream change: relationship_reference_limits_match_oracle|GH-1534: bounded receipt changes refusal advice 377 to 434 with edge-limit 1; retain missing-reference caps and exact accounting."
  "2026-10-27T00:49:15.107Z",codex-sol,"Implemented GH-1534 kernel ordering, edge reservation, skip-and-continue edge packing, versioned producer cursors and independent bounds receipts; implemented GH-1535 complete active-population test-health scope and counts. Added focused kernel and section regressions plus exact CLI differential cases for hidden failures and required-evidence pages. The PR had automatic merge enabled; disabled it to honor the explicit instruction to leave the PR unmerged."
  "2026-10-27T00:53:59.189Z",codex-sol,"Updated the native compatibility constant and exact crash-harness oracle guard/receipt/remedies to 2026.10.23, preserving strict version rejection. Current README pin references are refreshed; the October 21 receipt is explicitly historical. just changelog-check passes unchanged because changelog generation uses its separate pinned tool pair and this task remains open."
  "2026-10-27T00:55:18.376Z",codex-sol,"Focused native validation: cargo test --locked --lib --all-features orientation_ passed 59 tests, failed 0. New regressions cover required endpoint ordering, continuation and legacy-policy refusal, oversized-edge skip, direct-edge reservation and complete active test-health counts under hidden focus. No oracle comparison was weakened or skipped."
  "2026-10-27T00:57:43.760Z",codex-sol,"Live comparison of the published 2026.10.21 and 2026.10.23 kernels confirms GH-1534: with a-child parent root, root blocked_by z-blocker and nodeLimit 1, the former returns a-child with its parent edge; the latter returns z-blocker with its blocking edge. Both report one omitted node. A concurrent oracle reinstall invalidated the first standalone conformance and crash-check attempts through missing modules/version metadata; these are not pass evidence. The aggregate now runs alone against the restored locked installation. Linked tests are executed through pm; repository test-result tracking is disabled, so measured results are retained in comments."
  "2026-10-27T01:06:36.449Z",codex-sol,"The extra local health check identifies global package version skew and existing shared merge-driver drift, tracked on existing pm-rust-vuwe. Verifying the same tracked state in a disposable clone with isolated global state and clone-local drivers installed by the locked oracle, matching the CI setup. Shared clone configuration is unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T01:08:00.173Z",codex-sol,"CI-style project health verification passed with exit 0 in a disposable clone: installed merge drivers with the locked 2026.10.23 oracle, then ran node tests/oracle/launch.mts health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit under isolated global configuration. Only the two existing guidance/provenance advisories remain; authority is healthy. Shared local configuration drift is separate and tracked on pm-rust-vuwe."
  "2026-10-27T01:27:59.440Z",codex-sol,"Independent security gate: cargo audit passed with exit 0 and one existing allowed warning, RUSTSEC-2024-0449 for the unmaintained unsafe-libyaml dependency. No advisory configuration or dependency is changed. The broad aggregate and stable 34-case orientation differential suite remain running on the final source."
  "2026-10-27T01:39:51.117Z",codex-sol,"Stable full orientation attempt completed 32 passed, 2 failed. The existing large-edge-limit case hit its unchanged 5-second native child deadline under concurrent load and passes in a serial exact rerun (1 passed). The new population regression incorrectly assumed a one-token legacy budget could transport the result; the oracle correctly returns an output-budget refusal. Its population assertions now use the upstream integration pattern of explicit --output-budget unbounded, while an additional exact bounded-refusal comparison is retained. No existing oracle test or deadline was weakened. The aggregate reached its 2400-second local linked-test deadline after 15 completed suites; remaining stages require separate or hosted evidence."
  "2026-10-27T01:40:45.551Z",codex-sol,"Correction to the population-test refinement: explicit --output-budget controls are outside the current native context command slice, so the new population matrix uses supported 800 and 8000 token budgets with focus limits 1 and 10. This still exposes the hidden failing item and complete active denominator, with exact oracle bytes and independent semantic assertions. The one-token bounded refusal is checked separately. The unit regression also checks an empty packed focus against a nonempty active test population. No existing comparison or supported command contract is reduced."
  "2026-10-27T01:45:19.814Z",codex-sol,"Final population regression passes (1 passed, 0 failed), using the native-supported --depth deep surface, focus limits 1 and 10, token budgets 4000 and 8000, and a separate exact one-token refusal comparison. Together with the serial large-edge-limit pass, all 34 distinct orientation tests are verified across the 32-pass full run and focused reruns; this is not a claim that the earlier complete command was green. The broad local aggregate completed 15 suites with 511 passing tests before its 2400-second linked-test timeout. Library coverage and the stable crash harness are being checked separately."
  "2026-10-27T01:47:08.088Z",codex-sol,"Final static checks pass: cargo fmt --all -- --check and cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings. Library-only branch-instrumented validation passes 348 tests. Measured src/orientation_deps.rs, src/orientation_deps/packet.rs and src/orientation_context/sections.rs each have 100 percent lines, functions, regions and branches. Whole-library totals are 98.3607 percent lines, 97.7496 percent functions, 98.5884 percent regions and 99.2089 percent branches; this library-only run is not the repository aggregate coverage gate. Source documentation and changelog checks already passed. The 34 distinct orientation cases pass across the full attempt and focused reruns, including the final native-supported deep-context population test."
  "2026-10-27T01:54:27.971Z",codex-sol,"Class **(b), upstream regression or undocumented contract change**: after killing\na published update at its first per-task `rename`, a published restart comment\nreturns successfully with 2026.10.21 but exceeds the unchanged 15-second external\ndeadline with 2026.10.23. Both use the existing crash harness's frozen `Date`\npreload and live elapsed time. The retained item lock belongs to a dead process.\nThis is evidence about that deterministic fixture; it does not establish a hang\nunder an ordinary advancing wall clock.\n\nAn independent probe of both installed packages measured 2026.10.21 returning\nexit 0 in 559 ms, and 2026.10.23 reaching the 15-second deadline. The project\noracle remains pinned to 2026.10.23. No native recovery behavior or harness\ndeadline is changed to imitate or accept the timeout.\n\nMinimal Linux reproduction from the package root, with the locked oracle\ninstalled (use a separate 2026.10.21 installation for the control):\n\n```bash\nrepo=$PWD\noracle=$repo/tests/oracle/node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli\nwork=$(mktemp -d)\ncd \"$work\"\npm_oracle=(env HOME=\"$work/isolated-home\" UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE=1\n  NODE_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1 PM_SENTRY_DISABLED=1\n  PM_TELEMETRY_SOURCE_CONTEXT=test DO_NOT_TRACK=1 LC_ALL=C TZ=UTC\n  node --import \"$repo/scripts/crash-clock.mts\" \"$oracle/dist/cli.js\")\n\"${pm_oracle[@]}\" init --defaults --prefix crash- --agent-guidance skip --json --no-extensions\n\"${pm_oracle[@]}\" create Task \"Synthetic crash probe\" --id crash-probe \\\n  --description \"Acknowledged synthetic write\" --create-mode progressive \\\n  --author conformance-agent --json --no-extensions\nstrace -f --kill-on-exit -qq -o kill.trace -e trace=rename \\\n  -e inject=rename:signal=SIGKILL:when=1 -- \"${pm_oracle[@]}\" \\\n  update crash-probe --description \"Interrupted synthetic write\" \\\n  --author conformance-agent --json --no-extensions\ntimeout --signal=KILL 15s \"${pm_oracle[@]}\" comment crash-probe \\\n  \"Restart synthetic sentinel\" --author conformance-agent --json --no-extensions\n```\n\nExpected: the preserved restart command recovers the dead writer and returns\nexit 0, as observed with 2026.10.21. Actual with 2026.10.23: no response before\nthe external deadline. The original five crashing-harness failures all report\nthis timeout rather than an accepted recovery result. Targeted upstream issue\nsearches found no matching frozen-clock/rename restart report; the orchestrator\nshould confirm deduplication and file this reproduction upstream."
  "2026-10-27T01:57:15.990Z",codex-sol,"Verification handoff: all 11 original orientation failures are intentional release changes and are ported; 34 distinct orientation tests pass across the complete attempt and focused reruns. Final formatting, Clippy, source documentation, changelog, audit and isolated project health pass. The three changed implementation modules have 100 percent line/function/region/branch coverage in a 348-test library run. The full aggregate is not green locally: 511 tests in 15 suites passed before its 2400-second deadline; the stable crash harness is 77 passed and 5 timeout failures. An independent two-version control proves the additional published frozen-clock restart change, tracked by pm-rust-oracle-frozen-restart with minimal commands and expected/actual outputs. Push the ported changes on PR #122, retain the 2026.10.23 oracle and unchanged recovery assertions, and leave both items blocked for upstream/orchestrator review. No item is closed and no merge is authorized."
